          "Comments" -> {
           "Software" -> 
            "Created with the Wolfram Language : www.wolfram.com", 
            "Creation Time" -> 
            DateObject[{2026, 4, 19, 11, 44, 50.}, "Instant", "Gregorian", 
              None]}|>],
       Selectable->False],
      DefaultBaseStyle->"ImageGraphics",
      ImageSize->500,
      ImageSizeRaw->{1800., 399.84},
      PlotRange->{{0, 1800.}, {0, 399.84}}]},
    {
     PaneBox[
      StyleBox["\<\"Figure 3. A cartogram driven by a hand-curated \
Association of 19 G20-ish economies; every other country appears in grey and \
does not contribute to the density field, but still visibly deforms because \
diffusion is global.\"\>",
       StripOnInput->False,
       FontFamily->"Helvetica",
       FontSize->10,
       FontSlant->Italic],
      Alignment->Center,
      ImageSize->500]}
   },
   DefaultBaseStyle->"Column",
   GridBoxAlignment->{"Columns" -> {{Center}}},
   GridBoxItemSize->{"Columns" -> {{Automatic}}, "Rows" -> {{Automatic}}},
   GridBoxSpacings->{"Columns" -> {{Automatic}}, "Rows" -> {{0.6}}}],
  "Column"]], "Output",
 CellMargins->{{66, 20}, {10, 14}},
 ShowCellLabel->False,ExpressionUUID->"a9c77fd8-f9cf-4cf2-a0e8-1f96304ed8af"],

Cell["8. Implementation notes", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"e5262c52-e06a-4f4c-bb68-8437d4b9c685"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "\[Bullet] ",
 "Only the diffusion is done in Fourier space; advection uses NDSolveValue's \
RK45 stepper over the reconstructed velocity. Modes below a relative \
tolerance (",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox["10", 
    RowBox[{"-", "3"}]], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",ExpressionUUID->
  "c3872901-72ed-4dd4-af99-db0e04090860"],
 " by default) are considered extinct, giving ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox["t", "\[Star]"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",ExpressionUUID->
  "46c949fd-3f61-43b8-a012-2b3bbe493fe9"],
 ".\n\[Bullet] ",
 "Speed mode replaces the per-sub-step inverse DCT with a linear \
interpolation between 60 log-spaced density/gradient snapshots, giving \
sub-pixel agreement with Quality at ~7\[Times] the throughput. Switch to ",
 StyleBox["PerformanceGoal -> \"Quality\"", "Input"],
 " when you need bit-exact reproduction.\n\[Bullet] ",
 "Heavy-tailed metrics (Monaco on population density, Luxembourg on GDP per \
capita) produce enormous per-cell densities that can destabilise the \
advection. ",
 StyleBox["WorldCartogram", "Input"],
 " clamps values at a configurable fraction of the mean and caps the \
rasterised grid at a multiple of the positive-cell mean.\n\[Bullet] ",
 "Long country edges are densified before being transformed, matching ",
 StyleBox["shapely.segmentize", "Input"],
 " on the Python side of this project.\n\[Bullet] ",
 "The algorithm is grid-convention-compatible with the Python implementation \
so the two are drop-in interchangeable for debugging / cross-validation."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"3dcce137-2c69-4a55-ad48-186ef3ad678b"],

Cell["9. References", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"86090615-b306-4188-b6d8-9de34055f334"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "\[Bullet] M. T. Gastner & M. E. J. Newman, \"Diffusion-based method for \
producing density-equalizing maps\", ",
 StyleBox["PNAS",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 " ",
 StyleBox["101",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 "(20), 7499\[Dash]7504 (2004). ",
 ButtonBox["doi:10.1073/pnas.0400280101",
  BaseStyle->"Hyperlink",
  ButtonData->{
    URL["https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.0400280101"], None}],
 ".\n\[Bullet] ",
 "Source code and the Python twin:\n        ",
 ButtonBox["github.com/mthiel74/Contiguous-Cartograms",
  BaseStyle->"Hyperlink",
  ButtonData->{
    URL["https://github.com/mthiel74/Contiguous-Cartograms"], None}],
 ".\n\[Bullet] ",
 "Relies on Wolfram's ",
 StyleBox["CountryData", "Input"],
 ", ",
 StyleBox["GeoGraphics", "Input"],
 ", ",
 StyleBox["FourierDCT", "Input"],
 ", and ",
 StyleBox["NDSolveValue", "Input"],
 "."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"21130c5f-584b-435d-a329-87a4158cbfe9"]
},
